# Correct the Mercadona and LIDL products that hold the weight of a piece as a
# fixed size, and split the six products that hold two Mercadona pieces each
# (backend plan 0244, section 7). post.sh runs `node kilo-pieces.js` inside the
# harvester pod, because a queue row decides every group and the harvester
# already speaks to catalog over NATS. Each change is an ordinary item update
# or create, with the harvester's actor, one catalog transaction per product.
# No price changes anywhere.
#
#   7.1  a sized Mercadona piece sold by the kilo becomes KILOGRAM with no size,
#        and its old size becomes its approximate weight
#   7.2  a sized piece priced as one (Mercadona label `ud`, LIDL "Aprox.")
#        becomes UNIT with no size and keeps its old size as its weight
#   7.3  prints how many kilo pieces still wait for a weight from the next run
#   7.4  each product with two or more ACTIVE Mercadona rows sold by weight
#        keeps the row with the lowest price per kilo, and each other row gets
#        a new product of its own
#
# THIS TASK IS DISARMED. Both windows say `never`, so no deploy runs it, the
# runner records nothing for it, and a merge cannot stop a deploy. The owner
# arms it in a commit that states:
#
#   - RUN_UNTIL_STAGING and RUN_UNTIL_PRODUCTION, each a UTC date. A window is
#     at most 14 days after the commit that writes it, which is how long a dump
#     is kept, so write the dates in the pull request that ships the release.
#   - PRODUCTION_RELEASE, the version of the velista release that carries the
#     catalog columns of plan 0244 and kilo-pieces.js. Uncomment its line.
#   - the six ceilings below.
#
# Staging held the same data as production on 2026-11-04, because it is the
# production copy of 2026-11-03. So staging rehearses the task on real data
# first, and its window should close before the production one opens.
# The deploy unit whose release runs this task (k8s plan 0015 D9).
UNIT="velista"
RUN_UNTIL_STAGING="never"
RUN_UNTIL_PRODUCTION="never"
# PRODUCTION_RELEASE="<the version, such as 0.18.0, without its v>"
DATABASES="catalog harvester"
#
# The most products, per group, that the task may change. check.sh counts them
# with `--count` and refuses above these numbers, and post.sh counts again and
# passes them to the command as `--max-kilo`, `--max-piece` and `--max-split`,
# which refuses too. An empty value is not a number, so both scripts refuse it.
#
# THE OWNER STATES THEM. Plan 0244 section 7.5 proposes 200 sized pieces sold
# by the kilo (7.1), 20 sized pieces priced as one (7.2) and 10 merged products
# (7.4). The counts read on 2026-11-04 were 131, 7 plus 6, and 6, in both
# clusters. Confirm the proposal or write other numbers after reading the count
# that the check phase prints, never to get past it.
MAX_KILO_STAGING=""
MAX_KILO_PRODUCTION=""
MAX_PIECE_STAGING=""
MAX_PIECE_PRODUCTION=""
MAX_SPLIT_STAGING=""
MAX_SPLIT_PRODUCTION=""
